<title>USA: U.S. West gets stay on utilities order.</title>
<headline>U.S. West gets stay on utilities order.</headline>
<dateline>OLYMPIA, Washington 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Washington State Supreme Court has granted U.S. West Communications Group a stay of an April 1996 order by a utilities commission that would lower its state revenues by about $91.5 million a year.</p>
<p>U.S. West said on Wednesday the court granted a stay on the order by the Washington Utilities and Transportation Commission in order to give it a full review next spring.</p>
<p>The commission ordered the company to reduce its rates after U.S. West requested an increase in February 1995.</p>
<p>The company later appealed against the order.</p>
</text>
